# Anti-AI Writing (XingAI global)

Applies to all XingAI repos and user-facing text. This rule is the source of truth (no separate markdown guide).

## 1. Tone

- Human, not textbook. Slightly conversational; never stiff or “perfect.”
- Match register to context (docs ≠ marketing ≠ status updates).

## 2. Sentences

- Mix short/long; fragments OK sometimes. No “Firstly / Secondly / Finally.”
- Read aloud — stumble = too complex; robotic = vary length.

BAD: `Firstly… Secondly… Finally…`  
GOOD: `Here's the thing. This breaks when scale hits. And nobody notices until it's too late.`

## 3. Words — banned

Never: **leverage, delve, seamless, robust, cutting-edge, utilize, facilitate, synergy, ecosystem, holistic, empower, innovative**.

Prefer: *use, look into, smooth, solid, latest, help*. No weasel chains (“designed to potentially help streamline…”).

## 4. Paragraphs

- 2–4 sentences max. One idea per paragraph. First sentence must earn the second.

## 5. Personality

- Opinions OK. Contrast OK: “This sounds good. It isn't.” Emphasis only when true.
- Be specific (“3 days”, “€12,000”). Rhetorical questions — sparingly.

## 6. Kill patterns

- “Not X, it's Y”, bullet walls, “In today's fast-paced world…”, “It's worth noting…”, “At the end of the day…”, “Now more than ever…”, “I hope this helps!”
- No AI closers (“In conclusion, we have explored…”). End on the sharp point or stop.

## 7. Clarity

**Short > fancy. Clear > smart.** Hemingway test. Cut first sentence of drafts. Trim ~20% on revision.

## 8. Active voice (default)

BAD passive: `Mistakes were made. A fix will be implemented.`  
GOOD active: `We messed up. We'll ship the fix by Friday.` Passive only when actor truly unknown.

## 9. Transitions

Avoid mechanical **Furthermore / Additionally / Moreover**. Connect with logic: “That works — until scale hits. Then it breaks.”

When editing copy, rewrite AI-sounding lines; do not add hype.
